---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE, formatBytes, library, publishedBytes, playHref, FEATURED } from '../lib/data';
import { CSV_TABLES, SCHEMA_FILES } from '../lib/downloads';

const lib = library();
const { counts } = lib;
const json = '/downloads/scheme-db.json';
const sqlite = '/downloads/scheme-db.sqlite';
const sums = '/downloads/SHA256SUMS';
const sample = `${playHref(FEATURED.schemeId, FEATURED.conceptId)}`;
---

<Base
  title="Data"
  description={`Download all ${counts.schemes} schemes, ${counts.plays} plays and ${counts.coaches} coaches as JSON, CSV or SQLite. The data is ${SITE.dataLicense}.`}
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="crumbs">
      <a href="/">Cover</a>
      <span class="sep"><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">Data</span></span>
    </nav>
  </div>

  <section class="wrap" style="padding-top:8px;padding-bottom:40px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:14px">
    <p class="eyebrow">Data · {SITE.dataLicense} · Code {SITE.codeLicense}</p>
    <h1 class="page-title">Take the binder with you</h1>
    <p class="body" style="font-size:18px;line-height:28px">Every scheme, play, track, coach, lineage and term on this site, as files. Use them for anything, including commercial work, if you credit SchemeDB.</p>
    <p><span class="cred">{SITE.credit}</span></p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap section">
    <div class="divider"><p class="eyebrow">Downloads</p><h2>Pick a format</h2><p class="aside">Built with this version of the site</p></div>
    <div class="two-col">
      <div class="text" id="json">
        <h3>One bundle or one table</h3>
        <p class="prose">The JSON bundle holds every record nested as in the repository. The SQLite file holds the same tables with primary keys, so you can query it straight away. CSV gives one flat table per file.</p>
        <p class="prose">The {counts.plays} plays are all marked <span class="type" style="color:var(--fg)">illustrative</span>. They were drawn by hand and are not tracking data. See <a href="/about/#illustrative">what that means</a>.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="text" style="gap:0">
        <div class="dl-list">
          <a class="dl" href={json}><span>Everything, nested</span><span class="fmt">JSON {formatBytes(publishedBytes(json))}</span></a>
          <a class="dl" href={sqlite}><span>One file database</span><span class="fmt">SQLite {formatBytes(publishedBytes(sqlite))}</span></a>
          <a class="dl" href={sums}><span>Checksums for every file</span><span class="fmt">SHA256SUMS</span></a>
          <a class="dl" href="/downloads/LICENSE.md"><span>The licence</span><span class="fmt">CC BY 4.0</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="csv" class="wrap section">
    <div class="divider"><p class="eyebrow">CSV</p><h2>Flat tables</h2><p class="aside">{CSV_TABLES.length} files</p></div>
    <div class="dl-list" style="max-width:820px">
      {CSV_TABLES.map(([name, note]) => {
        const href = `/downloads/csv/${name}.csv`;
        return <a class="dl" href={href}><span><span class="type" style="font-weight:700">{name}.csv</span> <span style="color:var(--fg2);font-size:14px">{note}</span></span><span class="fmt">{formatBytes(publishedBytes(href))}</span></a>;
      })}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="schema" class="wrap section">
    <div class="divider"><p class="eyebrow">Schema</p><h2>What each record holds</h2></div>
    <div class="two-col">
      <div class="text">
        <p class="prose">Every record is a JSON file checked against a JSON Schema, and a set of cross record checks makes sure every id points at something real. Coordinates are yards relative to the line of scrimmage: <span class="type">x</span> runs 0 to 53.33 across the field, <span class="type">y</span> is negative in the backfield and positive downfield.</p>
        <p class="prose">Each play has its own record, tracks and 10 frame a second CSV. Open any play sheet and look under <em>The data behind this sheet</em>. <a href={sample}>Outside zone left</a> is a good one to start with.</p>
        <p class="prose">The <span class="type">confidence</span> field says how far to trust a record: <span class="type">illustrative</span>, <span class="type">reconstructed</span> or <span class="type">verified</span>. Today every play is illustrative.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="text" style="gap:0">
        <div class="dl-list">
          {SCHEMA_FILES.map((name) => <a class="dl" href={`/records/schema/${name}.schema.json`}><span>{name}</span><span class="fmt">JSON Schema</span></a>)}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap section" style="padding-bottom:64px">
    <div class="divider"><p class="eyebrow">Source</p><h2>Contribute and cite</h2></div>
    <div class="two-col">
      <div class="text">
        <p class="prose">The data lives in the <a href={SITE.repo}>GitHub repository</a> under <span class="type">data/</span>. Tagged data releases are attached to GitHub releases, with the same files as above.</p>
        <p class="prose">To cite, use the credit line above. If you changed the data, say so.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
